WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.784
Welcome. This is your ten-day plan for early math.

2
00:00:03.234 --> 00:00:11.131
The goal is a child who counts a group by touching each thing once, knows which number is more, and adds two small groups up to ten.

3
00:00:11.731 --> 00:00:17.419
That is the goal. It is not a promise. Day ten is a check, and it shows you where your child is.

4
00:00:18.219 --> 00:00:23.019
This plan is for a child who can say the numbers, but loses track when counting.

5
00:00:23.469 --> 00:00:29.138
Often one thing gets counted twice, or one gets skipped, and the answer changes each time.

6
00:00:29.588 --> 00:00:33.831
Or the counting is fine, but putting two groups together is not there yet.

7
00:00:34.281 --> 00:00:39.442
It is a normal step. Children learn these things at different times between four and six.

8
00:00:40.242 --> 00:00:44.871
Saying the numbers is not the same as counting. Counting is three small rules.

9
00:00:45.321 --> 00:00:46.462
Touch each thing once.

10
00:00:46.912 --> 00:00:48.522
Say one number for each touch.

11
00:00:48.972 --> 00:00:50.680
And the last number tells how many.

12
00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:55.984
Here is what is inside. Ten days. One page a day, about ten minutes.

13
00:00:56.434 --> 00:01:01.579
Day one is a short check. It shows you where to start. Day ten shows you what changed.

14
00:01:02.029 --> 00:01:04.853
Every day has a short video like this one, for you.

15
00:01:05.303 --> 00:01:11.908
And every day starts with real things on the table. Buttons, blocks or dry pasta. Then the page.

16
00:01:12.608 --> 00:01:16.952
Days two, three and four are counting, numbers to ten, and more and less.

17
00:01:17.402 --> 00:01:21.520
Day five is a halfway check. It tells you to go on, or to go back.

18
00:01:21.970 --> 00:01:25.953
Then the parts of five, adding, the partners of ten, and counting on.

19
00:01:26.403 --> 00:01:31.049
Day ten is the final check, with sums your child has never seen in the book.

20
00:01:31.849 --> 00:01:38.336
Here is how each day works. First, watch that day's video. Scan the code on the page with your phone.

21
00:01:38.786 --> 00:01:43.354
Then read the yellow box at the top of the page. It gives you three short steps.

22
00:01:43.804 --> 00:01:48.043
Do the first job together, with real things. That takes about two minutes.

23
00:01:48.493 --> 00:01:52.562
Then your child carries on with the page, and shows you three things at the end.

24
00:01:53.362 --> 00:01:59.294
You need the printed pages, a pencil, crayons, scissors, and about ten small things to count.

25
00:01:59.744 --> 00:02:04.832
When you are ready, start with day one. It is a short check, and it takes about four minutes.
